  <h2 id="sales">Who pays for these skills, and how they judge you</h2>

  <p>
    Employers and clients pay for skills that solve problems. They judge you by results, reliability and fit.
  </p>
  <p>
    The first basic skill is writing down what you value and why.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ai">AI and passion vs purpose vs pay in career choice: which tasks are under pressure</h2>

  <p>
    AI tools can structure comparisons and suggest questions. Routine comparison gets easier.
  </p>
  <p>
    Honest self-assessment and accountability hold value. A staged path helps: now, use AI to structure options; later, test them in real work.
  </p>

